@broadcast "The Last Lot"
@category shopping
@length 240
@type scripted

::actors
@actor npc_lot_vosk
@alias npc_lot_vosk VOSK
@actor npc_lot_operator
@alias npc_lot_operator YOLANDA
::endactors

::asset the_last_lot_logo

▛▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▜
▌      T H E   L A S T   L O T      ▐
▌   everything must go. it did.     ▐
▙▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▟

::endasset

::asset lot_price_card

┌────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  LOT 41 · WINTER COAT, LONG, GREY      │
│  PREVIOUS OWNERS: 1 (TECHNICALLY)      │
│                                        │
│      WAS ₵340      NOW ₵89             │
│                                        │
│  CALL NOW · 3 REMAINING · NO RETURNS   │
└────────────────────────────────────────┘

::endasset

::scene OPEN

ROOM zone_studio_1782953094650

EVENT FADE_IN

MUSIC last_lot_theme
♪ A game-show sting that has been sold twice and repossessed once. ♪
MUSIC_END

TITLE the_last_lot_logo

CAM 1 WIDE sales_floor

SHOT
A rotating display plinth under hard white light. Behind it, shelving stacked to the ceiling with unlabelled crates. A phone number sits burned into the bottom of frame, slightly crooked, and has been for years.
SHOT_END

ENTER npc_lot_vosk

VOSK:
Welcome back to The Last Lot, where everything must go — and I want to stress that most of it already has.

ACTION npc_lot_vosk pats the plinth twice, the way a man pats a horse he is about to sell.

VOSK:
I'm Rennie Vosk. For the next two hours, I am going to put things in front of you, and you are going to decide how much your dignity costs.

::scene LOT_41

CAM 2 CLOSEUP plinth

TITLE lot_price_card

LOWER_THIRD
LOT 41 — WINTER COAT
₵89 · 3 REMAINING
LOWER_THIRD_END

SHOT
A long grey coat turns slowly on the plinth. It is genuinely a very good coat. There is a neat, professionally repaired hole below the left shoulder blade.
SHOT_END

VOSK:
Lot forty-one. Wool blend, storm-lined, deep pockets. Retail three-forty. Today: eighty-nine.

VOSK:
One previous owner.

ACTION npc_lot_vosk holds up a single finger, and then, after a beat, lowers it.

VOSK:
Technically.

VOSK:
Now — you're looking at the repair. Everybody looks at the repair. I want you to look at the STITCHING on the repair. That is craftsmanship. Somebody cared about this coat.

VOSK:
Somebody cared about this coat more than they cared about the previous owner, and I think that's beautiful.

::scene PHONES

CAM 3 MEDIUM phone_bank

ENTER npc_lot_operator

YOLANDA:
Rennie, I've got a caller on line two asking whose coat it was.

VOSK:
Tell them it's THEIR coat now, Yolanda. That's the magic of retail.

YOLANDA:
They're asking if it's cursed.

VOSK:
Nothing on this programme is cursed. Several items are HAUNTED, and those are clearly marked.

ACTION npc_lot_operator covers the receiver and says something we do not hear.

YOLANDA:
They'll take two.

VOSK:
They'll take two! Two coats for a man who does not know how many arms he's going to need. That is FORWARD PLANNING.

::scene LOT_42

CAM 2 CLOSEUP plinth

SHOT
The coat is replaced by a sealed grey pallet, shrink-wrapped, with a Precinct 9 evidence tag still stapled to the corner.
SHOT_END

VOSK:
Lot forty-two. Municipal surplus. Sealed pallet, mixed contents, sold as seen — and I do mean AS SEEN, because I haven't seen it either.

VOSK:
Could be tools. Could be somebody's whole life in a box. Could be forty kilos of one specific thing.

VOSK:
That happened last month. Somebody in Meltwater Row now owns every left boot in the district.

YOLANDA:
He's called back twice.

VOSK:
He has called back twice, and both times he sounded FINE.

::scene LOT_43

CAM 1 WIDE sales_floor

SHOT
Two attendants wheel out a full-height clone vat, empty, drained, lit from within. It hums. Nobody wheeling it makes eye contact with it.
SHOT_END

VOSK:
And our big lot of the hour. Ex-display. One owner, and this time I mean that sincerely.

VOSK:
Fully functional, fluid system flushed, only cosmetic wear to the door seal. You have seen these in clinics at nine thousand.

VOSK:
Today — and I am going to get in trouble for this — twelve hundred.

YOLANDA:
Rennie, they want to know why it's cheap.

VOSK:
Because the man who ordered it is not in a position to collect it, Yolanda.

ACTION npc_lot_vosk spreads his hands, entirely at peace.

VOSK:
That is the ENTIRE reason. There is no other reason. That is the business we are in.

::scene CLOSE

CAM 2 MEDIUM vosk

OVERLAY
THE LAST LOT

CALL COLDWATER 4-4-LOTS

NO RETURNS · NO PROVENANCE · NO QUESTIONS THAT HELP
OVERLAY_END

VOSK:
Two hours a day, this is what the Basin leaves behind. And somebody's got to sell it, or it just sits there reminding everybody.

VOSK:
Might as well be you wearing it. Might as well be warm.

TICKER
THE LAST LOT · All lots sold as seen · No returns, no exchanges, no provenance provided or implied · Municipal surplus is sold post-forfeiture and cannot be reclaimed by prior holders or their estates · Restored persons may not claim property forfeited by a previous body · Items marked HAUNTED are sold under the same terms as items that are not · The management does not know what is in the pallets
TICKER_END

MUSIC last_lot_theme
♪ The sting plays out, cheerful and completely unbothered. ♪
MUSIC_END

CREDITS 5
THE LAST LOT
Presented by Rennie Vosk. Phones by Yolanda.
Lot 41 is still available.
END_CREDITS

EVENT FADE_OUT

END
